  "slug": "coding-rnas-generates-6c5b",
  "summary": "New portals, workflows and knowledge networks target reproducible reuse of spatial and single-cell data, from HuBMAP's 9,316 datasets to cohort-level pipelines.",
  "synthesis": "Most items build infrastructure for harmonizing and reusing spatial and single-cell data, rather than introducing new inference methods. The HuBMAP Data Portal hosts 9,316 public datasets from healthy human tissues. SpaceBlocks offers a Snakemake workflow for expert-supervised cohort-level spatial transcriptomics, and TRACE adds traceable curation, demonstrated in a harmonised single-cell glaucoma resource. NLM-CKN links cell phenotypes from 88 datasets and 10 organs to Cell Ontology, genes, diseases and drugs, while Gene Embedding Hub standardizes 67 human gene-embedding sets. PhenoMe and SENgEAR provide interactive exploration of microscopy embeddings and senescence signatures. QUEST, which virtually stains H&E to predict multiplex immunofluorescence, is a modeling contribution adjacent to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
